Subject: [PATCH] FLOWTRACE: the op log follows the IC data and every HT9050
 engine cursor -- EastSun 1007 '????????????????????????????????' (run on the
 real machine).

csystem.cpp: DoAllProcess calls W906_FlowTraceTick (end of file) first; one line -- run/stop/homed, IC on the loader tray (MMTrayY) / InArmSuck / FLCarryKit (In Shuttle 1) / FTestSuck (Index) / FRCarryKit (Out Shuttle) / OutArmSuck, and LoadTask_9050, iCatchFromLoader9050Task, iArmTask, iInArmPlaceToShuttleTask, AutoSHT1/2Task, iTestHeadMotorTask, iTestYFinePitchTask, iTestYFrontTask, iFrontTestSuckICTask, iFrontTestDestroyICTask, OutArmTask, iPickFromShuttle1Task -- goes to the op log as 'FLOW' only when it changed (g_W906FlowNote, set in tools/wb_serve.cpp W906_OpLogInit; 0 in ctests). Read only; the call replaces a blank line. W6_6_CSystemCycle, W6_6_Hub, Flow9050_Shuttle passed. Release linked; Debug compiled (link waits for EastSun's program). WORKLOG row 189.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
